---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_URL, CONTACT_EMAIL, publisher } from '../data/site';
const schema = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'AboutPage', name: `About ${SITE_NAME}`, url: `${SITE_URL}/about/`, publisher }];
---
<Base title={`About ${SITE_NAME} & Editorial Policy`} description="RecruitmentAI.org is an independent plain-English handbook on AI in recruiting. Who writes it, how it is funded, what it covers and how to request corrections." path="/about/" schema={schema}>
  <div class="wrap prose" style="padding:40px 24px">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › About</p>
    <h1>About {SITE_NAME}</h1>
    <p>{SITE_NAME} exists because “recruitment AI” is used to sell everything from a résumé parser to an autonomous agent, and the people affected (recruiters, hiring managers, founders and candidates) rarely get a plain explanation of the difference. The handbook explains what the software does, in the order a reader needs it, with no vendor funding.</p>
    <h2>Editorial policy</h2>
    <ul><li>We describe; we do not rank. The <a href="/vendors/">vendor landscape</a> groups products by what they automate. Readers who want rankings should use a review site.</li><li>No vendor pays for inclusion, placement or wording. There are no affiliate links.</li><li>Every claim about a product comes from its documentation, public materials or hands-on use. Pricing is summarised and approximate.</li><li>Legal content is general information, not advice; we cite the rule and recommend counsel.</li></ul>
    <h2>Disclosure</h2>
    <h2>Who writes it</h2>
    <p>The editors have worked in in-house talent acquisition, agency recruiting and recruiting-software product teams. Chapters are reviewed quarterly and when regulation or the market changes materially.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> for corrections, questions and suggestions for new chapters.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
